mportant historical  figures who each possessed a particular  skill and due to the successful  translation of the text featuring on the  Magnificent Stoneworks we know that they  represent none other than the mythical  seven sages a group of individuals who  repeatedly awaken in times of hardship  to help the hero and Princess fend off  the evil tormenting Hyrule many a Time  involving Ganondorf for his alter ego  Ganon it seems the ancient Garuda wanted  to memorialize the sages and thus they  erected these massive Stone monuments in  their honor although the existence of  the seven uncommon knowledge among the  present-taker rudo actual meaning  implication and history seem to have  been all but lost to the women of the  desert they don't know who each  individual statue represents nor do they  even refer to them as sages they're  ecologists think Garuda Town who studies  the monuments named rutana refers to  them as the Divine Protectors of the  Gerudo it even implies that Garuda  believed them to be all female warriors  even though the seven sages have  historically been a mix of many  different races and genders it shows  that while her research is slowly  progressing her deeper understanding is  still right with misinterpretation and  bias viewing them from the perspective  of the gorilla alone and not from high  rules combined history and culture this  is not surprising though of the ancient  and present-day Garuda are very  particular about the Memorial's  historical figures not only are they all  betrayed as female presumably in their  own image but they also left nameless  and are instead inscribed with poetry or  singular adjectives like fidget it's no  wonder why the identity of these figures  are eventually forgotten as the ages  creeped by the existence of the eight  Heron on the other hand seemed to be  completely unknown to the present-day  Garuda where at the very least written  off as nothing more than an urban legend  one description even mentions that the  remote section of the Highlands where  the statue resides is one that the  Garuda did not set foot in because of  the many dangers including the extreme  weather conditions as such none of the  Garuda who are alive today have ever  laid eyes upon the eighth heroine let  alone known who or what it is supposed  to personify when it comes to the  ancient Garuda however it is a different  story it's all but certain that they  were well aware of and ate heroine not  only are they the most likely candidate  for its construction seeing as the  architecture is close to identical to  the other seven but the Yeager clown  Hideout which is confirmed to be an  ancient crude archaeological site  features 8 similar looking statues  facing each other in a circle  likewise we can see that the seven  massive monuments tucked away inside the  desert have an empty space that would  have fit an eighth statue perfectly one  final detail about the eighth heroine is  that the sword they are supposed to  clench onto as seen on the other seven  is missing from the statue itself and  can instead be found Atop The Summit of  the Highlands not far away for what  reason no one knows for sure  so these are some of the basic facts  about the statues there is a bit more to  it but we'll cover those as we go along  given how few people seem to be aware of  the existence of the eighth heroine it's  hard to pinpoint its exact placement in  hyrule's history or which parts of the  rumors about it are true or false  especially when the culture that  supposedly built it seems completely  oblivious to it and thus cannot provide  us any insight I joked before about  Patricia but she's actually one of only  two beings in the world who mentioned  the eighth heroine by name through  dialogue the other being bosai you know  the creepy guy who tries to get into  Link's pants and gives you the quest to  seek out the statue not even the town  archaeologist who I remind you actively  studies the history of the seven  heroines every day ever even mentions  the rumors about an eighth statue in the  case of bosai I can understand why you  would know about it since he is a Hylian  he says he's been intrigued by the  stories of an eighth heroine ever since  he was a child so apparently it is a  legend that some hylians dare speak of  but how in the heck does the pet seal  belonging to the leader of the Gerudo  know about it and why has no one ever  caught on to the fact even the woman who  interprets her words of wisdom doesn't  even Flinch when mentioning the eighth  heroine look at her she's completely  unfazed I mean come on lady it's a  central part of your religion this would  be like if a Christian found out there  were secretly 11 Commandments but I  don't know Moses lost one on the way  down from the mountain anyway there's  two important details which have given  shape to many similar theories and  verdicts about the nature and identity  of the eighth heroine first is to claim  that as stated before the statue itself  as well as the person it embodies have  been wiped clean from history and second  is a quest lock that says that despite  being lost in memory she is still  worshiped to this day by her faithful in  the Gerudo highlands now the only  faction we know that lives in the  highlands are of course the yiga who  have been fiercely loyal to Ganon ever  since they seceded from the Chica 10 000  years ago the fact that the eighth  heroine has been wiped from history yet  is still worshiped by what is  essentially a Ganon cult has led many to  believe that this individual could have  been on the wrong side of history and  possibly involved in some some nefarious  act perhaps a sage gone Rogue who  betrayed the other seven or as some  suggest it may even be a memorial to  Ganon himself why else with the yiga of  all people pay homage to this forgotten  Idol there's a piece of NPC dialogue  that reiterates the same basic concept  as the quest log except here instead of  calling them her faithful it instead  refers to them as the people who hang  around the Gerudo Highlands which  further reinforces that this would  indeed have to be the yiga as day and  day alone fit the description the game  generally doesn't refer to things like  Monsters or Wildlife as people there is  however one problem one that has plagued  the Zelda series for decades and  continues to do so here localization  differences the original Japanese text  never actually refers to these mystery  worshipers as her faithful nor as the  people who hang around the grudo  highlands it simply says her followers  instead on the surface this may seem  like a very minor difference but for a  theory this can have massive  repercussions the English text Advocates  that these devotees are human beings  which inadvertently eliminates any  alternatives because like I said as far  as people go there are none who hang  around these parts in the present day no  one but the eager well in link but he  doesn't count meanwhile the Japanese  text keeps it ambiguous after all  followers can apply to anyone really  anyone who's sentient anyway I believe  that this tiny seemingly harmless  translation difference may just be  responsible for limiting our perspective  on the mystery of the eighth heroine  since what if this isn't referring to  the yiga at all but instead someone else  the yiga have never been a very logical  choice to me despite the English texts  insisting that they are they don't seem  to concern themselves at all with the  reverence of ancient monuments  especially those belonging to other  cultures in fact they appear to be  completely indifferent even downright  disrespectful towards them for example  the statues located in their Hideout  which features the eighth one all have  their face dishonorably covered in  drapes which displays their Insignia no  doubt intended as a giant middle finger  to the Gerudo who they are still at war  with they do the same thing to chica  Idols too by the way I see no evidence  that they held these monuments in any  sort of high regard so why would they  venture out into the frigid coal to  worship this one sure their Hideout is  in the highlands but it's still quite  the expedition to get to the eighth  heroine another aspect that potentially  works against the yiga is the extreme  secrecy behind the statue as well as the  timeline of events what's quite  distinctive about the Statue is that  unlike the side of the seven heroines it  doesn't feature a shika Shrine the  ancient chica constructed their shrines  all over Hyrule in the most obscure  secretive older sites imaginable find an  ancient ruin chances are there's going  to be a shrine nearby even instructors  that stem from the time of Skyward Sword  which is an insanely long time ago so  why not here could it be that even the  shika from 10 000 years ago were  oblivious to the ace statue if so how  would the yiga know where it is let  alone who the statue represents the clan  didn't form until after the Calamity of  ten thousand years ago when the king of  Hyrule started persecuting the shika in  their technology if we stick by the  Japanese text and assume that these  so-called followers are not necessarily  human beings more options suddenly  become available and one in particular  stands out as a prime candidate for me  especially in context with the sequel an  intelligent being who's not only present  in the highlands but one that actually  visits the area in and around the eighth  heroine frequently despite originating  from the fahren region the lightning  Spirit farage has two secondary flight  paths one at Lake hylia and the other  sees it snaking around the Gerudo  Highlands drifting in from the southern  part of the mountain range right past  the Forgotten sword makes its way close  to the top of the statue then travels in  between the statue and the sword after  which it curves back around the summit  for subsequent visits until finally  taking off into the heavens at some  point but it gets even better because  now take a look at the flight path of  dinroll the fire dragon from the Elden  region after spawning and passing along  the back of the volcano it heads  Southwest then makes a straight shot  through the canyon towards the Cliffside  where the statue is located until it too  decides to call it a day and head for  the clouds I'd say it almost looks like  it's on a pilgrimage of sorts the only  dragon who doesn't exert a similar  behavior is Nedra and while that does  somewhat weaken the argument for a  statue worshiping ceremony by the  dragons we do have to keep in mind that  Nedra has been incapacitated by Ganon  for what we can presume to be a  considerable amount of time before link  wakes up from his stasis and depending  on the order in which you explore Hyrule  it remains trapped on the mountain until  link finally cures its Affliction a  valid enough excuse to skip daily  service for a while I suppose with that  said what could the ancient dragon  spirits who have been around since time  immemorial possibly wand with a statue  like this well that all depends on what  the secret identity behind this Monument  is if it is someone they knew well or as  the in-game text suggests if followed it  would make perfect sense for the dragon  spirits to pay their respects to them  especially if that individual died or  sacrificed themselves for a greater  purpose in the distant past as mighty  images stick as the dragon Smith appear  they are not above Gods sages  contemporary Spirit guardians or other  types of deities in Skyward Sword for  example they control parts of their  respective provinces but did so in the  service of goddess hylia who appointed  them to protect the surface in her  absence and here's where another major  difference in the localization comes  into play the nickname of the eight  heroine we have been reiterating  throughout the video is actually not  accurate to the original Japanese name  there it is the carpet giant goddess you  can see the impact of omitting a single  word as it makes a world of difference  as opposed to just another Sage this  statue is hinted to be a tribute to a  goddess of source which is not nearly on  the same level as a sage this brings us  to the latest footage for tears of the  Kingdom the figure depicted on a mural  definitely fits the characteristics of a  deity they appear to reside high in the  heavens suspended on a floating platform  with rays of light shining down upon  them more importantly the seven all  black artifacts that surround them could  reinforce a connection between this  entity and seven other beings the other  mentioned sages perhaps just like we see  with the statues eight in total with one  different from the rest speaking of  differences there's one more feature  about the eighth statue we haven't  mentioned so far it's not just that the  material is different and the sword is  missing but it also happens to be a  mirrored version of the other seven  monuments and lo and behold what do we  see on the mural two depictions of the  same symbol but mirroring each other one  on the side of what is presumably to be  an incarnation of Zelda and which  matches the symbol on the orbs and the  mirror opposite on the side of this  deity figure a coincidence it definitely  could be but if it is it is a very  interesting coincidence if this theory  is correct and the dragons are indeed  the ones worshiping the eight heroine  statue instead of the yika naturally  obvious candidate to shoot for will be  goddess highly given the history between  her and the dragon spirits and it very  well could be but we certainly shouldn't  rule out all the possibilities as well  there's a good chance that this is a  brand new deity whom we have never seen  or met before  let's wrap up the video with a final  piece of conjecture one that my guest  speaker may not resonate with so I want  to make it clear that these are my  thoughts and mine alone whoever or  whatever this creature on the mural ends  up being chances are we probably won't  get any decisive answers until we  actually you know play Tears of the  Kingdom in that sense the mystery behind  the eighth heroine remains for now  however I do have a strong conviction  that this character and the 8th heroine  are likely one and the same there's just  too many overlapping themes and  coincidences for me to ignore in fact I  would take it a step further and say  that the spectral being who has  Ganondorf pinned down and sealed deep  underground may also be connected to it  it definitely has a spiritual out of  this world kind of look and feel to it  so maybe the green Hand That Remains is  what's left of this ancient deity the  figure on the mural is shown to be  pretty huge in comparison to a regular  human or at least compared to Zelda if  this is indeed her now look at the size  comparison between Link's hand and the  one belonging to this entity it's like  twice the size whatever this creature  used to be it too must have been and  pretty big when link absorbs the green  energy The Entity seems to pass its  Essence down to the hero which explains  why he can suddenly conjure up these  almost god-like powers like the ability  to control time or become incorporeal  and move through solid matter in context  with today's subject it would also  clarify why this individual has been  completely forgotten over the course of  history perhaps long ago they sacrificed  their very existence to keep ganondorf's  physical body from being set loose upon  Hyrule once again they were then  memorialized in stone by the Ancients  but as the years crept by the memory of  their sacrifice and even their very  identity was slowly lost a time which is  a common occurrence in the land of  Hyrule it only took ten thousand years  for the Calamity to completely Fade Into  myth which mind you was a huge battle  involving giant robots and whatever  transpired back when Ganondorf was still  human clearly took place much much  longer ago  and that wraps up today's video if you  liked it please be sure to check out  Conrad's video as well over on his  channel the Commonwealth realm and if  you didn't be sure to check out Conrad's  video over on his channel regardless  because it may be way better than mine a  special Thanks goes to larulia historian  for providing me with the Japanese texts  and of course to my mods Discord  community patreons and channel members I  will see you all in the next video this  is Don signing off and have a good one  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  foreign  [Music]  foreign

